Goal
Design a deterministic data model and integration plan that fits the existing architecture without duplicating data or embedding unrelated entities inside Activity or Week.
Feature 1: Activity reflection
When a user marks an activity as done, display a sheet that captures subjective session data.
The reflection must:
exist as its own persistent entity,
reference the associated activity by ID,
not be embedded directly inside the activity model unless the existing architecture strongly requires it,
support zero or more physical discomfort reports.
Proposed activity reflection fields:
ActivityReflection
- id
- activityID
- feel
- sessionRPE
- performanceNotes
- createdAt
- updatedAt
Feature 2: Weekly reflection and week completion
Add a “Complete Week” action at the bottom of the week view.
Before completion:
check whether every planned activity is either done or skipped,
if unresolved activities remain, show the user which activities are incomplete,
allow the user to return and close them individually,
or explicitly mark all unresolved activities as skipped after confirmation.
Once all activities are resolved:
collect weekly reflection data,
persist a weekly reflection as its own entity,
reference the associated week by ID,
mark the week complete only after the weekly reflection is saved.
Proposed weekly reflection fields:
WeeklyReflection
- id
- weekID
- weekRating
- fatigue
- recovery
- sleepQuality
- motivation
- mood
- lifeStress
- whatWentWell
- nextWeekChanges
- createdAt
- updatedAt
Do not duplicate calculated weekly totals inside the reflection.
Feature 3: Physical discomfort
Physical discomfort must be modeled as an ongoing issue that can span multiple activities and weeks.
A physical issue is not owned by an activity or a week.
Proposed persistent entities:
PhysicalIssue
- id
- bodyArea
- side
- startedAt
- status
- resolvedAt
- optionalTitle
- optionalNotes
ActivityIssueReport
- id
- physicalIssueID
- activityID
- activityReflectionID
- painLevel
- timing
- trendDuringActivity
- createdAt
WeeklyIssueReview
- id
- physicalIssueID
- weekID
- weeklyReflectionID
- weeklyTrend
- resultingStatus
- createdAt
Physical issue lifecycle
When discomfort is entered during an activity reflection:
Ask for body area and side.
Search active physical issues with the same area and side.
Let the user attach the report to an existing issue or create a new issue.
Never automatically assume two reports are the same issue.
Never create a duplicate PhysicalIssue for every activity report.
At weekly reflection:
Pull active physical issues relevant to the week.
Show each issue’s reports from that week.
Ask whether the issue worsened, stayed stable, improved, or resolved.
Only mark an issue resolved through explicit user action.
Resolving an issue must preserve all historical reports and reviews.
